Relevant columns and why they matter  
• `CytoConverted.RefNo / CaseNo / InvNo / Clone` – identify the unique clone we are studying.  
• `CytoConverted.ChrOrd` – numeric chromosome (11, 13, 17) that lets us filter by chromosome.  
• `CytoConverted.Start`, `CytoConverted.End` – genomic interval; we check whether it overlaps the co‑ordinates given in the task.  
• `CytoConverted.Type` – whether the segment is a Gain or a Loss.  
• `KaryClone.RefNo / CaseNo / InvNo / CloneNo` – joins a clone coming from CytoConverted to its karyotype line.  
• `KaryClone.CloneShort` – short karyotype description we finally want to show.  

Conditions to locate the three required alterations for the same clone  
1. Loss on chr 13 that overlaps 48 303 751‑48 481 890  
  `ChrOrd = 13 AND Type = 'Loss'  
  AND Start <= 48481890 AND End >= 48303751`  
2. Loss on chr 17 that overlaps 7 668 421‑7 687 490  
  `ChrOrd = 17 AND Type = 'Loss'  
  AND Start <= 7687490 AND End >= 7668421`  
3. Gain on chr 11 that overlaps 108 223 067‑108 369 102  
  `ChrOrd = 11 AND Type = 'Gain'  
  AND Start <= 108369102 AND End >= 108223067`  

Below are ten progressively more complex BigQuery queries (all SELECT‑only, no DDL/DML) that explore and finally answer the task.  
Every query is enclosed in a ```sql``` block and limited to 20 rows except the final one.

```sql
-- 1. Look at chr13 Loss segments that overlap the requested window
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, ChrOrd, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 13
  AND Type = 'Loss'
  AND Start <= 48481890
  AND End   >= 48303751
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect chr17 Loss segments in the small region on 17p
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, ChrOrd, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 17
  AND Type = 'Loss'
  AND Start <= 7687490
  AND End   >= 7668421
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect chr11 Gain segments covering 11q22.3
SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone, ChrOrd, Start, End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
WHERE ChrOrd = 11
  AND Type = 'Gain'
  AND Start <= 108369102
  AND End   >= 108223067
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Clones that have BOTH chr13‑Loss and chr17‑Loss
SELECT DISTINCT a.RefNo, a.CaseNo, a.InvNo, a.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS a
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS b
  ON  a.RefNo  = b.RefNo
  AND a.CaseNo = b.CaseNo
  AND a.InvNo  = b.InvNo
  AND a.Clone  = b.Clone
WHERE a.ChrOrd = 13 AND a.Type = 'Loss'
  AND a.Start <= 48481890 AND a.End >= 48303751     -- chr13 window
  AND b.ChrOrd = 17 AND b.Type = 'Loss'
  AND b.Start <= 7687490  AND b.End >= 7668421      -- chr17 window
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Clones with chr13‑Loss AND chr11‑Gain
SELECT DISTINCT a.RefNo, a.CaseNo, a.InvNo, a.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS a
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS b
  ON  a.RefNo  = b.RefNo
  AND a.CaseNo = b.CaseNo
  AND a.InvNo  = b.InvNo
  AND a.Clone  = b.Clone
WHERE a.ChrOrd = 13 AND a.Type = 'Loss'
  AND a.Start <= 48481890 AND a.End >= 48303751     -- chr13 window
  AND b.ChrOrd = 11 AND b.Type = 'Gain'
  AND b.Start <= 108369102 AND b.End >= 108223067   -- chr11 window
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Clones with chr17‑Loss AND chr11‑Gain
SELECT DISTINCT a.RefNo, a.CaseNo, a.InvNo, a.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS a
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS b
  ON  a.RefNo  = b.RefNo
  AND a.CaseNo = b.CaseNo
  AND a.InvNo  = b.InvNo
  AND a.Clone  = b.Clone
WHERE a.ChrOrd = 17 AND a.Type = 'Loss'
  AND a.Start <= 7687490 AND a.End >= 7668421       -- chr17 window
  AND b.ChrOrd = 11 AND b.Type = 'Gain'
  AND b.Start <= 108369102 AND b.End >= 108223067   -- chr11 window
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Using EXISTS to insist that ALL THREE events occur in a single clone
SELECT DISTINCT c.RefNo, c.CaseNo, c.InvNo, c.Clone
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS x
    WHERE x.RefNo  = c.RefNo  AND x.CaseNo = c.CaseNo
      AND x.InvNo  = c.InvNo  AND x.Clone  = c.Clone
      AND x.ChrOrd = 13 AND x.Type = 'Loss'
      AND x.Start <= 48481890 AND x.End >= 48303751
)
AND EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS y
    WHERE y.RefNo  = c.RefNo  AND y.CaseNo = c.CaseNo
      AND y.InvNo  = c.InvNo  AND y.Clone  = c.Clone
      AND y.ChrOrd = 17 AND y.Type = 'Loss'
      AND y.Start <= 7687490 AND y.End >= 7668421
)
AND EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS z
    WHERE z.RefNo  = c.RefNo  AND z.CaseNo = c.CaseNo
      AND z.InvNo  = c.InvNo  AND z.Clone  = c.Clone
      AND z.ChrOrd = 11 AND z.Type = 'Gain'
      AND z.Start <= 108369102 AND z.End >= 108223067
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Bring in karyotype information for any clone that satisfies all three conditions
SELECT DISTINCT
  c.RefNo, c.CaseNo, c.InvNo, c.Clone,
  k.CloneShort
FROM (
    /* same EXISTS filter as query #7 */
    SELECT DISTINCT RefNo, CaseNo, InvNo, Clone
    FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
    WHERE EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
        WHERE RefNo  = CytoConverted.RefNo
          AND CaseNo = CytoConverted.CaseNo
          AND InvNo  = CytoConverted.InvNo
          AND Clone  = CytoConverted.Clone
          AND ChrOrd = 13 AND Type = 'Loss'
          AND Start <= 48481890 AND End >= 48303751
    )
    AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
        WHERE RefNo  = CytoConverted.RefNo
          AND CaseNo = CytoConverted.CaseNo
          AND InvNo  = CytoConverted.InvNo
          AND Clone  = CytoConverted.Clone
          AND ChrOrd = 17 AND Type = 'Loss'
          AND Start <= 7687490 AND End >= 7668421
    )
    AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted`
        WHERE RefNo  = CytoConverted.RefNo
          AND CaseNo = CytoConverted.CaseNo
          AND InvNo  = CytoConverted.InvNo
          AND Clone  = CytoConverted.Clone
          AND ChrOrd = 11 AND Type = 'Gain'
          AND Start <= 108369102 AND End >= 108223067
    )
) AS c
LEFT JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.KaryClone` AS k
  ON  k.RefNo   = c.RefNo
  AND k.CaseNo  = c.CaseNo
  AND k.InvNo   = c.InvNo
  AND k.CloneNo = c.Clone
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Examine the chromosomal intervals for the three regions side‑by‑side
SELECT DISTINCT
  a.RefNo, a.CaseNo, a.InvNo, a.Clone,
  a.ChrOrd AS Chr13_ChrOrd, a.Start AS Chr13_Start, a.End AS Chr13_End,
  b.ChrOrd AS Chr17_ChrOrd, b.Start AS Chr17_Start, b.End AS Chr17_End,
  c.ChrOrd AS Chr11_ChrOrd, c.Start AS Chr11_Start, c.End AS Chr11_End
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS a           -- chr13 loss
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS b           -- chr17 loss
  ON  a.RefNo  = b.RefNo  AND a.CaseNo = b.CaseNo
  AND a.InvNo  = b.InvNo  AND a.Clone  = b.Clone
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c           -- chr11 gain
  ON  a.RefNo  = c.RefNo  AND a.CaseNo = c.CaseNo
  AND a.InvNo  = c.InvNo  AND a.Clone  = c.Clone
WHERE a.ChrOrd = 13 AND a.Type = 'Loss'
  AND a.Start <= 48481890 AND a.End >= 48303751
  AND b.ChrOrd = 17 AND b.Type = 'Loss'
  AND b.Start <= 7687490  AND b.End >= 7668421
  AND c.ChrOrd = 11 AND c.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c.Start <= 108369102 AND c.End >= 108223067
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: complete list of clones that show ALL THREE alterations,
--     with the genomic coordinates for each and the karyotype (CloneShort)
SELECT DISTINCT
  c13.RefNo,
  c13.CaseNo,
  c13.InvNo,
  c13.Clone            AS CloneNo,
  -- chr13 loss coordinates
  c13.ChrOrd           AS Chr13_ChrOrd,
  c13.Start            AS Chr13_Start,
  c13.End              AS Chr13_End,
  -- chr17 loss coordinates
  c17.ChrOrd           AS Chr17_ChrOrd,
  c17.Start            AS Chr17_Start,
  c17.End              AS Chr17_End,
  -- chr11 gain coordinates
  c11.ChrOrd           AS Chr11_ChrOrd,
  c11.Start            AS Chr11_Start,
  c11.End              AS Chr11_End,
  -- karyotype description
  k.CloneShort
FROM `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c13   -- chr13 loss
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c17   ON
  c13.RefNo  = c17.RefNo  AND c13.CaseNo = c17.CaseNo
  AND c13.InvNo = c17.InvNo AND c13.Clone = c17.Clone
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.CytoConverted` AS c11   ON
  c13.RefNo  = c11.RefNo  AND c13.CaseNo = c11.CaseNo
  AND c13.InvNo = c11.InvNo AND c13.Clone = c11.Clone
JOIN `mitelman-db.prod.KaryClone` AS k         ON
  k.RefNo   = c13.RefNo
  AND k.CaseNo  = c13.CaseNo
  AND k.InvNo   = c13.InvNo
  AND k.CloneNo = c13.Clone
WHERE
  -- chr13 Loss window
  c13.ChrOrd = 13 AND c13.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c13.Start <= 48481890 AND c13.End >= 48303751
  -- chr17 Loss window
  AND c17.ChrOrd = 17 AND c17.Type = 'Loss'
  AND c17.Start <= 7687490 AND c17.End >= 7668421
  -- chr11 Gain window
  AND c11.ChrOrd = 11 AND c11.Type = 'Gain'
  AND c11.Start <= 108369102 AND c11.End >= 108223067;
```

